@startuml
title SOL payment and access: target flow for an already prepared server
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 220
hide footbox

actor Provider
participant "Provider Bash script\n(planned)" as Setup
actor Owner
participant "Dashboard + wallet\n(planned)" as Browser
participant "Devnet RPC" as RPC
participant "Billing/access program\n(planned)" as Program
participant "Treasury" as Treasury

group One-time setup, before payment
  note over Provider, Program : Linux server is already installed, configured, and recoverable.
  Provider -> Setup : Run manually: register owner and fixed terms
  Setup -> RPC : Provider-signed register_server
  RPC -> Program : Execute registration
  Program -> Program : Create ServerRecord + unpaid Subscription
end

group Owner purchase or intentional renewal
  Owner -> Browser : Connect wallet and view server
  Browser -> RPC : Read finalized server + access state
  RPC --> Browser : Price, term, expiry, grants
  Owner -> Browser : Approve purchase / renewal
  Browser -> Browser : Create payment ID, sign transaction,\npersist pending metadata before submission
  Browser -> RPC : Submit owner-signed purchase_access / renew_access
  RPC -> Program : Execute signed instruction
  group Atomic payment and access update
    Program -> Program : Validate signer, enabled server,\naccounts, treasury, unused payment ID
    Program -> Treasury : Transfer exact SOL amount via System Program
    Program -> Program : Write receipt; extend subscription + owner grant
  end
  Browser -> RPC : Read finalized receipt + subscription/grants
  RPC --> Browser : Finalized payment and current access state
  Browser -> Browser : Verify program ownership and payment bindings
  Browser --> Owner : Payment result, expiry, SSH instructions
end

note over Browser, RPC
  On timeout or reload, reconcile the same payment ID first.
  A callback or transaction signature alone is not payment proof.
  Retry only after resolving the previous transaction; never pay again just because it timed out.
end note
note over Owner, Program
  SSH login is separate: sign a fresh message, then the daemon reads finalized access.
  No order database or payment-triggered server preparation.
end note
@enduml
